Package: ubuntu-iceland-device
Version: 0.2.20
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Ubuntu iceland port contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Depends: systemd, kmod, e2fsprogs, util-linux, cloud-guest-utils,
 systemd-zram-generator, alsa-ucm-conf, alsa-utils, pipewire, pipewire-pulse,
 wireplumber, swh-plugins
Description: Device support for the OnePlus Pad 4 (iceland)
 Board-specific integration for the OPD2514 running an Ubuntu userspace on
 the Perpetua mainline kernel:
 .
  * root filesystem discovery: the initramfs conf.d that points
    initramfs-tools at LABEL=UBPAD4_ROOT, because the stock vendor_boot
    cmdline carries no root= and is deliberately never rewritten;
  * first-boot root filesystem expansion to the whole userdata partition;
  * two-tier swap: zstd-compressed zram in front of the storage;
  * speaker protection: PipeWire filter-chain "Speakers" (HPF, stock-tone EQ,
    SC4 compressor, -1 dBFS look-ahead limiter via swh-plugins), raw sink
    demoted, protected sink set as the configured default (A6);
  * audio userspace: the Pad 4 UCM2 profile (speakers at the stock 0 dB
    bring-up cap, internal mics at stock levels) and the WirePlumber
    soft-mixer rule, in front of the AudioReach topology the firmware
    overlay ships.
  * audio service discovery: the userspace protection-domain mapper and
    name service (protection-domain-mapper, qrtr-tools) are masked, because
    the kernel's own qcom_pd_mapper serves this SoC and the userspace one,
    which only knows the ADSP root domain here, answered first on about
    one boot in fourteen and left the audio domain unpublished (no sound
    card until the next reboot).
 .
 This package grows the way its gts9u counterpart did: one integration at a
 time, each added only when the matching regression has been observed on this
 hardware.  Hardware enablement lives in the kernel and in the firmware
 overlay; this package only carries userspace integration.
